1. WHY THIS SOURCE IS PUBLISHED

tokenstat's central claim is about what happens to your data: what is read,
what is kept, and what may leave the machine. A claim like that is worth
nothing if it cannot be checked. The application source is published so that
anyone can read it and verify the claim for themselves.

It is published to be *audited*, not to be reused. That is the whole of the
intent, and the permission below is scoped to exactly that.


2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

You may:

  (a) read, study and analyse this source code;
  (b) copy it as needed to do so, for example by cloning the repository;
  (c) compile it privately in order to verify that a published build
      corresponds to this source, or to satisfy yourself about its behaviour;
  (d) discuss and describe what you find, including publicly, and including
      quoting portions of it where that is necessary to make a point.

Nothing here restricts fair use, fair dealing, or any other right you have
under applicable law, and nothing here restricts your rights in the GPL-3.0
portions of this repository.


3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Without written permission from pueev OÜ, you may not:

  (a) distribute, publish, sublicense or sell this source code or any part of
      it, whether modified or not;
  (b) distribute or publish a build produced from it, whether modified or not,
      by any means, including any app store or software marketplace;
  (c) create and distribute a derivative work based on it;
  (d) use it, or a build of it, to provide a service to third parties;
  (e) remove or alter this notice.

Private modification for your own inspection under section 2 is permitted. It
is publication that is reserved, not curiosity.


